# Cloudflare Pages headers. Conservative, safe hardening only (behavior-preserving:
# the previous Vercel site set no custom headers on static assets). API functions
# set their own CORS headers in code.
# Strict CSP for the two pages that carry the licence KEY (in the /activate
# fragment and rendered into the DOM) or the session-id BEARER credential
# (/signal/success URL). default-src 'none' + connect-src 'self' means that even
# if a script were somehow injected it could not exfiltrate the key to any
# external host, and no external script can load at all. These pages set
# noAnalytics, so — unlike the rest of the site — they need no PostHog origins.
# 'unsafe-inline' is required (the pages use inline <style>/<script>), but the
# pages have no injection sink (textContent + encodeURIComponent only), so the
# real value here is locking script/connect to same-origin. Google Fonts + the
# data: favicon are the only external resources these pages use.
/activate*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/signal/success*
  Content-Security-Policy: default-src 'none'; script-src 'unsafe-inline'; style-src 'unsafe-inline' https://fonts.googleapis.com; font-src https://fonts.gstatic.com; img-src 'self' data:; connect-src 'self'; base-uri 'none'; form-action 'self'; frame-ancestors 'none'

/*
  X-Content-Type-Options: nosniff
  Referrer-Policy: strict-origin-when-cross-origin
